- EBS Volume
	- Elastic Block Store Volume
	- Network drive attached to an instance
	- Allows data to persist even after termination of an instance
	- Mounted to one instance at a time. At ccp level
	- Bound to specific availability zones.
	- Like network usb sticks.
	- Network Drive (not a physical drive)
		- it uses the network to communicate to instance. so might have a delay
		- it can be detached from one instance and attached to another one relatively quickly.
		- Its locked to AZ
			- it means an EBS volume in us-east-1a can not be used int us-east-1b
			- you need to snapshot a volume to move it.
		- It needs provisioned capacity that is size in GBs, and IOPS(Operations per seconds)
			- billed for this
			- can be increased
		- Can be left unattached.
		- Delete on Termination attribute
			- Allows for deletion of volume when instance is terminated.
				- By default root EBS is deleted when root is deleted

