- Scalability means that an application / sytem can handle greater loads by adapting
	- There are two kinds of scalability:
		- Vertical
		- Horizontal (= elasticity)
	- Scalability is linked but different from High Availability.
- ## Vertical Scalability
	- Vertical means increasing the size of the instance
	- For Example
		- If application is running on t2.micro then scaling up will man running it on a t2.large
	- Very common for non distributed systems such as DB
	- Hardware limit
- ## Horizontal Scalabiltiy
	- It means increasing the number of instances/ systems for your application
	- Horizontal implies distributed systems
	- Common for web applications / modern applications
	- It is easy to do thanks to the cloud
- ## High Availability
	- Usually goes hand in hand with horizontal scaling
	- Means running your app / system in at least 2 AZs
	- Goal is to survive a data center lose due to disaster
